; Leg BB -- PORTING.md SS16af leg AH repeated, FOR THE HOST CLOCK.
;
; Block check 1.  The floor, and the other half of the calibration: the
; quantity being calibrated is AG-minus-AH, which SS16af could only say was
; "one clock quantum".  BB is what makes BA's number a difference rather
; than an absolute.
;
; Targets to reproduce, from SS16af leg AH (Victor clock):
;     rxfull 0, rxpeak 2,585, rxbytes 37,534, 18 packets, 0 resends,
;     elapsed 2,700 cs.
;
; A NULL RESULT AGAINST AH IS THE PASS.  Nothing has changed on the block-1
; path since AH ran, so a leg that comes back materially different is
; measuring the harness and not the port -- and would invalidate BA too,
; since BA-minus-BB is the whole deliverable.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 1
log packets s16ahBB.pkt
send rcvbb.dat
statistics
